femto patch for iri-string 0.7.15
Subject: template: decode the triplet that follows undecodable triplets

In reserved and fragment expansion ({+var}, {#var}) a value is decomposed into
characters, plain text and percent-encoded triplets. When a triplet shows that
the triplets before it are not UTF-8 (`%C2` followed by `%00`), the decoder
gave up those triplets but kept the new one without looking at it. If that
triplet is a character by itself, the next triplet found a complete character
followed by more bytes in the buffer, and an assertion failed
("`decoded` buffer contains at most one character"). At the end of the value
the kept triplet was reported as undecodable although it is a character.

Decode the head of the buffer in one place (DecoderBuffer::take_decoded) and
call it again after undecodable triplets are given up, so the buffer never
holds a complete character or an undecodable triplet between two pushes. The
assertion is gone because the function no longer assumes it.

femto expands templates from OPDS catalog servers with a keyword typed by the
reader; the keyword `%C2%00%8A` with `{+query}` stopped the reader.

